---
source: crates/daemon/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: stdout
---
Grade the mail already in this mailbox against labelled scenarios: how often today's rules agree on who sent it, which mode it goes to and whether it makes a record; for what an email asks of you, precision and recall per kind of ask and how often the amount, due date and counterparty are exactly right; and every email they get wrong. Read-only and local. Run `mxr demo` first to get mail with labels

Usage: mxr classify eval [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --set <SET>
          Which labelled set to grade against

          Possible values:
          - quick: The labelled demo mail and every near-miss twin
          - full:  Every labelled email in the mailbox: on the 50,000-message demo, the labelled demo mail and all of the generated mail, with held-out phrasings reported on their own line. Takes up to a minute

          [default: quick]

      --account <ACCOUNT>
          Limit to one account; the default covers every account

      --format <FORMAT>
          [possible values: table, json, jsonl, csv, ids]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
